From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: spi: set the IPM duplex mode for raw transfers

mtk_spi_hw_init() zeroes SPI_CFG3_IPM_REG, with a note that only spi-mem
uses the register, and the spi-mem path does set it per operation. The
raw mtk_spi_fifo_transfer() and mtk_spi_dma_transfer() paths therefore
run every transfer in full duplex, and a one-way transfer has nothing
draining the other side.

On MT7988 SPI1 that stalls the engine once the 32 byte FIFO is full: the
BE14000 panel's init commands, which fit the FIFO, go through, and the
first 5120 byte pixel burst times out in mtk_spi_wait_for_transfer_done().
The same code works on MT7987, so the stall is a property of this IP.

The kernel driver selects the duplex mode before every transfer on IPM
hardware, half duplex with the direction of the one buffer present, or
full duplex when both are. Do the same in the two raw paths.

--- a/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/drivers/spi/mtk_spi.c
+++ b/plat/mediatek/apsoc_common/drivers/spi/mtk_spi.c
@@ -487,6 +487,29 @@ static void mtk_spi_setup_dma_addr(struc
 		       mdata->base + SPI_RX_DST_REG);
 }

+/*
+ * spi-mem sets CFG3 per operation, and mtk_spi_hw_init() zeroes it for the raw
+ * transfers below, which is full duplex. A one-way transfer then has nothing
+ * draining the other side, and on MT7988 SPI1 it never completes once the
+ * 32 byte FIFO fills. Pick the duplex mode per transfer, as the kernel does.
+ */
+static void mtk_spi_ipm_set_duplex(struct mtk_spi *mdata,
+				   const struct spi_transfer *xfer)
+{
+	uint32_t reg_val = 0;
+
+	if (!mdata->dev_comp->ipm_design)
+		return;
+
+	if (!xfer->tx_buf || !xfer->rx_buf) {
+		reg_val |= SPI_CFG3_IPM_HALF_DUPLEX_EN;
+		if (xfer->rx_buf)
+			reg_val |= SPI_CFG3_IPM_HALF_DUPLEX_DIR;
+	}
+
+	writel(reg_val, mdata->base + SPI_CFG3_IPM_REG);
+}
+
 int mtk_spi_fifo_transfer(struct spi_device *spi,
 				 struct spi_transfer *xfer)
 {
@@ -507,6 +530,7 @@ int mtk_spi_fifo_transfer(struct spi_dev

 	mtk_spi_reset(mdata);
 	mtk_spi_hw_init(mdata, spi);
+	mtk_spi_ipm_set_duplex(mdata, xfer);
 	if (xfer->speed_hz > spi->max_speed_hz)
 		xfer->speed_hz = spi->max_speed_hz;
 	if (xfer->speed_hz == 0)
@@ -581,6 +605,7 @@ int mtk_spi_dma_transfer(struct spi_devi

 	mtk_spi_reset(mdata);
 	mtk_spi_hw_init(mdata, spi);
+	mtk_spi_ipm_set_duplex(mdata, xfer);

 	if (xfer->speed_hz > spi->max_speed_hz)
 		xfer->speed_hz = spi->max_speed_hz;
